      "text_1": {
       "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
       "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "valter.toffolo@macnicadhw.com.br",
       "text": "<p><b>What is Ambarella CVflow architecture?</b></p>\r\n<p>CVflow is Ambarella’s computer vision chip architecture. Unlike a general-purpose CPU or GPU, it uses a dedicated vision processing engine programmed with a high-level algorithm description. That design scales performance to trillions of operations per second at very low power.</p>\r\n<p><b>Which neural network frameworks do Ambarella SoCs support?</b></p>\r\n<p>Customers map CNNs trained with industry-standard tools such as Caffe, TensorFlow, and PyTorch onto Ambarella processors. The CNN toolkit also covers ONNX. Detection, classification, and related CNN/DNN tasks run on-chip.</p>\r\n<p><b>Which Ambarella SoCs are used for ADAS?</b></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0;\">CV2FS is for front-facing stereovision ADAS cameras and computer-vision ECUs at L2+ and higher, with CVflow AI and ASIL C compliance. CV22FS targets forward-facing monocular ADAS cameras and similar ECUs, also with ASIL C. Ambarella uses ISO 26262 processes for functional safety–certified products used in ADAS and autonomous driving.</p>\r\n<p><b>What makes Ambarella a low-power edge AI SoC choice?</b></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0;\">The SoCs and CPUs are built for embedded edge platforms such as battery-powered cameras. They can outperform competing solutions on power efficiency, sometimes by 5× or more, while matching or beating results. Compression also cuts bandwidth and storage.</p>\r\n<p><b>What does stereovision add for robotics?</b></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Stereo processing turns a 2D view into a 3D scene and can detect generic obstacles the system was not trained to recognize. CV2 is positioned for accurate 3D environmental modeling, real-time neural network performance, advanced robotics, and industrial autonomous robots.</p>\r\n",
       "jcr:lastModified": "Sat Sep 26 2026 02:07:01 GMT+0000",
       "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/text",
       "textIsRich": "true"
      }
     }
    },
    "container_2": {
     "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
     "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/container",
     "backgroundColor": "rgb(247,247,247)",
     "title_1": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:title": "Ambarella N1 Family - Edge GenAI Is Here",
      "type": "h2",
      "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/title"
     },
     "text_1": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "text": "<p>Ambarella’s N1 family of Edge GenAI SoCs delivers the processing power needed to run multimodal large language models (LLMs), vision-language models (VLMs), and traditional CNN networks locally, without cloud dependency. Designed for autonomous mobile robots, on-premise AI boxes, smart city security, industrial automation, and intelligent healthcare, the N1 series sets a new benchmark for AI performance per watt at the edge.</p>\n<p>As an authorized Ambarella distributor and value-added engineering partner, Macnica Americas provides component supply, design-in support, and technical consulting to help you bring your next N1-based design to production.</p>",
      "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
     },
